 took over as the leader of Wakanda  he wanted to be Black Panther again but  he doesn't want to interfere with  sharees reign obviously he solves this  problem by going to the secret  necropolis under the Golden City so that  he can talk to bast the cat goddess you  know pretty standard cat stuff to give  him a new purpose she made him king of  the dead with all the strength and  wisdom of every black panther before him  who better to lead a team of superheroes  back to the land of the  I am a scarred reborn infinity wars  shocks aren't limited to the end of the  movie right at the beginning we find out  that Thanos and the Black Order killed  all the Asgardian refugees that Thor  worked so hard to save in Ragnarok that  might not be the end of Asgard though in  the comics Ragnarok isn't the end of the  world it's the end of a cycle as gods  Thor and the other s Guardians are  creatures of mythology they live die and  are reborn in the new forms eternally  bound by their nature if we're following  that logic then the next major quest for  a Thor who's more powerful than ever  could be the rebuilding of Asgard by  tracking down the reborn souls of the  other gods including an all-new  all-different Loki the return of Korg me  and Valkyrie they couldn't really kill  the three best new movie characters of  2017 off screen between movies could  they until proven otherwise let's just  assume that Korg meet and Valkyrie  weren't on the refugee ship for some  reason maybe they were out scouting for  groceries or fighting the Skrulls  anything to get them back for next time  seriously if happy Hogan can be in like  six of these movies then Valkyrie needs  to be in at least ten Tony Stark  r.i.p a lot of moviegoers predicted we'd  be bidding a fond farewell to Robert  Downey jr. and infinity war that didn't  happen this time but it may have been  set up for Avengers for Doctor Strange  traded Thanos the time stone in exchange  for sparing Tony Stark's life that's  surprising first because Strange swore  an oath to protect it and second because  he did it knowing that if Thanos got the  stones he was going to kill half the  galaxy anyway even a strange and Stark  we're BFFs and not just dudes who didn't  actually seem to like each other there  is no way anyone should trade Iron Man's  life for uncountable trillions unless  shortly before that scene is the one  where strange uses the time stone to  take a peek at 14 million alternate  outcomes and says that the good guys  only win in one given the bargain he  makes you have to assume that the one  reality where Thanos is defeated has to  be the one where Tony Stark lives long  enough to do something to turn the tide  we're betting it's a heroic sacrifice  that's been building for 11 years  the all-new Iron Man Tony Stark might be  on the way out but Iron Man could stick  around it's just going to be Jim Rhodes  under the helmet instead like Sheree  this one follows the precedent set in  the comics before he was more machine  roadie was Iron Man from 1983 to 1985 it  also seems like a logical continuation  of the story he's the only one besides  Tony to fight in the Ironman armor and  the big airport battle in civil war left  him injured beating Starks tech to walk  that puts him in a very similar position  to the way Tony was back in his early  comics appearances when he needed his  armor to keep his heart beating  if Rhodey does take over that provides  proof of concept for the idea that the  MCU can continue after the departure of  big-name actors something that was  already done on a small scale when Don  Cheadle took over the role of Rhodey  from Terrence Howard next time keep  waiting for Adam warlock Adam warlock is  a huge part of the original Infinity  Gauntlet story while his role for the  most part is limited to standing around  in space watching the big battle go down  he actually winds up in possession of  the gauntlet itself at the end between  that and its imminent arrival being  teased in the post-credits scene of  guardians of the galaxy vol 2 it might  have been surprising that he didn't make  an appearance in infinity war  he's even the focal point of the comic  book crossover that gave the movie its  name if you're thinking they might have  saved him for the sequel though it  doesn't seem likely one of the few  movies to have actually been announced  for the next phase of Marvel movies was  guardians of the galaxy vol 3 with Adam  being set up as ayisha's genetically  engineered instrument of revenge it's  way more likely that he'll show up there  that leaves the role open for a  spacefaring hero who can explain  galactic conflicts and it seems pretty  obvious that it's going to go to Captain  Marvel who was summoned at the end of  infinity war by Nick Fury's cosmic  beeper that makes sense structurally  since Captain Marvel and ant-man in the  wasp are the only MCU movies coming out  between infinity war and adventures for  as much as we like Scott Lang he's not  the guy who's going to be getting  everyone up to speed on the kree-skrull  war Carol Danvers on the other hand has  experienced battling against and  wielding exactly the kind of cosmic  power that the heroes are going to  need to beat Thanos once and for all  that leaves the Guardians free to fly  back into their own movie and the only  question left is whether they'll fight  Adam warlock or the Magus who is Adam  warlock evil self from an alternate  future comic books can be pretty  complicated cat wolf at last will admit  that this one's pretty unlikely but if  infinity war has proven anything it's  that the Marvel movies can do anything  and make a billion dollars they've spent  ten full years and nineteen movies  getting to that point but they just put  out a movie about a giant purple man  trying to get his hands on magic space  rocks featuring characters like Proxima  midnight and the collector and a major  plot point was that a space dwarf made a  magic hammer out of a talking tree Rock  complaining but you have to admit that  stuff's pretty weird clearly there's  nothing stopping them from doing a movie  where Captain America becomes a  super-powered werewolf and delivers an  inspirational speech to a bunch of other  werewolves it might even make sense from  the moviemaking standpoint if Chris  Evans really wants to scale back his  acting work and devote his time to  remodeling his house then why not  replace him with the CGI Wolfman with an  indestructible shield it would  definitely be a weird direction to lift  from the comics but they already did the  part where Thanos starts turning people  into cubes there's no way a wolf is any  weirder than that thanks for watching  click the looper icon to subscribe to  our youtube channel plus check out all  this cool stuff we know you love to  [Music]
 

